# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env — it is gitignored.

# --- Anthropic -------------------------------------------------------------
# Create at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- DigitalOcean Gradient inference (optional) -----------------------------
# An alternative endpoint for the Anthropic Messages API. Empty means Anthropic
# directly, which is the default and a fully supported configuration — so the
# rollback for anything below is blanking a variable, never editing code.
#
# WHAT IT MOVES, and the one thing it does not.
#
# 1. **It moves every PYTHON model call**: the decision loop, the dreamer and
#    the conference. They reach the endpoint through a FORCED TOOL CALL rather
#    than through the server-enforced schema, because this endpoint accepts
#    `output_config` with HTTP 200 and silently ignores it — measured, not
#    assumed. Pydantic validates the tool payload on this side, so the numbers
#    still reject; what degrades is reliability rather than safety, and a reply
#    carrying no tool call at all fails the cycle rather than half-filling it.
#
#    **Name the models too, or it refuses at startup.** DECISION_MODEL_ID and
#    DREAM_MODEL_ID are below. Left unset they fall back to a Claude tier id,
#    which this endpoint calls by another name and 403s on this account's tier
#    — a guaranteed failure, so it is refused once rather than 96 times a day.
#    `docs/DROPLET_AI.md` has the fidelity table: which models actually hold
#    the real schema over repeated calls, which is not the same question as
#    which models are good.
#
# 2. **It does not move the three souls.** They run on Hermes as the `hermes`
#    user, which cannot read this file — it is owned by `mudhorn` at mode 600,
#    and that is the user split working rather than a problem to route around.
#    Their key is a second credential in the hermes account's own home, one
#    file per Hermes instance:
#        /home/hermes/inference.env          yoda + the armorer
#        /home/hermes/dreamer/inference.env  grogu
#    See deploy/README.md, "Pointing the souls at DigitalOcean".
#
# There is NO fallback in either direction. A key that is set but unusable
# refuses rather than quietly answering from Anthropic: that would run, bill
# the wrong account, and leave nothing on any surface saying which model
# produced the orders.
#
# A MODEL ACCESS KEY, never a DigitalOcean personal access token — a PAT
# controls the account and this box runs an agent with a shell. It is created
# by hand in the control panel (AI Platform → Serverless Inference); creating
# one through the API is retired and answers `{"id": "gone"}`. Serverless
# inference is PREPAID: a zero balance takes every agent surface dark at once
# and nothing here can see it, so set a billing alert in the same sitting.
DO_INFERENCE_KEY=
# Blank uses the documented endpoint, https://inference.do-ai.run. It is not
# the switch — set on its own it moves nothing, and the startup line says so.
DO_INFERENCE_BASE_URL=

# --- Alpaca (PAPER TRADING) ------------------------------------------------
# Create paper keys at https://app.alpaca.markets/paper/dashboard/overview
# A paper account needs only an email address — no SSN, ID documents or bank
# link. Those are required only for a live account, which this build refuses
# to run against.
ALPACA_API_KEY=
ALPACA_SECRET_KEY=

# Leave this true. The bot aborts at startup if it is false, and AlpacaBroker
# refuses to construct. Going live is a separate, deliberate decision — read
# docs/HANDOFF.md first.
ALPACA_PAPER_TRADE=true

# --- Data feeds ------------------------------------------------------------
# Both have free tiers. They are NOT equivalent in importance.
#
# Finnhub supplies the earnings calendar that RiskGate's news blackout reads.
# Leave it blank and that rule has no windows to check, so it never fires and
# the bot will happily open a position minutes before an announcement. The
# loop warns at startup when this is missing.
#   https://finnhub.io/register  (free tier: 60 requests/minute)
#
# Marketaux supplies headlines for Claude's context. Purely informational --
# it gates nothing, and running without it is a supported configuration.
#   https://www.marketaux.com/  (free tier: 100 requests/DAY, hence the
#   30-minute cache in src/bot/data/marketaux.py -- do not lower it)
FINNHUB_API_KEY=
# Posts from the accounts in config/rules.yaml under `social:`. CONTEXT ONLY —
# these reach Claude's prompt and never the risk gate.
#
# Reading timelines needs a PAID X tier; free access does not meaningfully
# allow it. Leave this blank and the feed is simply off, which is a supported
# configuration: the bot runs with slightly less context and nothing else
# changes. https://developer.x.com
X_BEARER_TOKEN=

MARKETAUX_API_KEY=

# --- Dashboard password ----------------------------------------------------
# Leave blank for the loopback deployment: bound to 127.0.0.1 and reached over
# Tailscale, nothing is published and there is nobody to authenticate.
#
# Set it and EVERY dashboard page requires a login. This is what makes it safe
# to expose the dashboard on a public URL, which is otherwise a live view of a
# brokerage account on the open internet.
#
# It belongs here and NEVER in the repository. `brand/` is public static files,
# so a password committed there is readable in the page source.
#
# The app cannot tell whether it is exposed — a Tailscale Funnel or a reverse
# proxy still arrives on loopback — so nothing will warn you later. Set this
# BEFORE exposing it, not after.
DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=

# --- Dashboard chat -------------------------------------------------------
# Separate from the password above, deliberately: viewing an account and
# driving an agent that can reach the broker are different privileges, and one
# secret must not grant both.
#
# Setting this is not sufficient on its own. Chat also needs the sudoers rule
# in docs/HERMES_SETUP.md section 2b, and mudhorn-web.service running without
# NoNewPrivileges/RestrictSUIDSGID, which both block sudo. Without those the
# panel appears and every question fails.
#
# Leave blank and the chat panel is hidden and POST /chat returns 404.
#
# Set it to any long random string to enable asking Hermes questions from the
# dashboard. Off by default because every other part of that page reports what
# happened, and this one acts. Requires Hermes installed: docs/HERMES_SETUP.md.
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
DASHBOARD_CHAT_TOKEN=

# --- Bot behaviour ---------------------------------------------------------
# haiku | sonnet | opus. Start on haiku: it is the cheapest and the risk gate,
# not the model, is what keeps the account safe.
#
# This picks one of three CLAUDE models and is ignored the moment the id below
# names one outright. It is also not enough on its own once DO_INFERENCE_KEY is
# set, for the reason in that section: a tier resolves to a Claude id, and that
# endpoint will not serve one to this account.
CLAUDE_TIER=haiku

# Name a model OUTRIGHT, overriding the tier. Empty means the tier, so a
# deployment that never set these behaves exactly as it always did.
#
# REQUIRED when DO_INFERENCE_KEY is set. Two separate settings because the loop
# wakes 96 times a day and the dreamer once, so the model that is right for one
# is not automatically right for the other — the loop wants a fast one that
# holds the shape, and the dreamer wants a patient one that can follow a causal
# chain two hops out.
#
# Pick from the fidelity table in docs/DROPLET_AI.md, which measured whether a
# model holds the REAL schema over repeated calls. Read what it does not
# measure as well: it grades the shape, never the reasoning, and a model can
# comply perfectly and propose nonsense. `scripts/agent_behaviour_live.py` is
# the harness for that half.
#
# A model with no prices on file still runs — its calls report an UNKNOWN cost
# rather than a zero, which is deliberate. An invented price is the same class
# of error as an invented indicator.
DECISION_MODEL_ID=
DREAM_MODEL_ID=

# Seconds between decision cycles. 900 = 15 minutes, which pairs with the
# 1-hour prompt cache (roughly four cache reads per write).
DECISION_INTERVAL_SECONDS=900
